 # bench-sleep-tool (benchmark fixture)
 
-A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool, written in the 0.1.1-era style
-(bare `cordis` cohort). The host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool, migrated to the dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2
+cohort (`@deepseek-ai/cordis`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm`).
+The 0.1.1-era bare-`cordis` / `dsh-tools` `ContentBlock` imports are gone.
+
+Configuration: the bundle row in `cordis.patch.yml` (or a profile's own
+`cordis.patch.yml` overriding the row) carries `maxDurationMs`, the cap for one
+sleep, and `defaultDurationMs`, the fallback when the model omits
+`duration_ms`. Documented defaults are 60000 ms and 0 ms.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
